# OpenSplice Community Edition 6.9 DDSI2 datagrams, captured from a
# ZeroDDS publisher's own metatraffic sockets while the OMG dds-rtps
# Test_Reliability_0 harness ran OpenSplice against it (XCDR1).
#
# OpenSplice's single DDSI2 service speaks for several participants it
# hosts on the same host: the application participant
# (7c6b09d4000002d000000001), an internal "services" participant
# (7c6b09d40000000400000001) and an internal "durability" participant
# (7c6b09d40000007d00000001) in frames 3/6, plus a second application
# instance and two more internal participants in frame 7. It bundles
# their submessages into one datagram and switches the attributed
# source with INFO_SRC (DDSI-RTPS 2.5 §8.3.7.9) instead of sending one
# datagram per participant.
#
# This is the fixture for the INFO_SRC receiver-state bug: before the
# fix, every submessage after an INFO_SRC in a bundled datagram (frames
# 3 and 7) was attributed to the RTPS header's own GuidPrefix instead
# of the prefix INFO_SRC names, corrupting the SEDP reader's per-writer
# sequence-number state and losing the application participant's real
# "Square" subscription (frame 4) to a stale delivery pointer left by
# the misattributed durability-participant samples.
#
# Twelve frames, in the order captured; relative time in seconds from
# the first frame. One destination-context comment per frame, then the
# UDP payload as hex, 16 bytes per line, from the RTPS magic to the
# last octet -- no host names or IP addresses: the host name in the
# PID_ADLINK_PARTICIPANT_VERSION_INFO strings and the IPv4 address in the
# SPDP locators are replaced with same-length placeholders ("host-00",
# 192.0.2.1, RFC 5737).

# --- frame 1  t=+0.000000s ---
